{%- comment -%}
  Makes the store installable as an app on a phone's home screen.

  iOS: Safari -> Share -> Add to Home Screen. The apple-* tags give it a proper
  icon, its own title under the icon, and full-screen launch with no Safari
  chrome. On iOS 26 every home-screen site opens this way anyway; these tags
  set what it looks like when it does.

  Android: the browser menu offers "Install app" from the manifest alone.
  Chrome's automatic install banner additionally needs a service worker that
  controls the page, which a Shopify theme cannot serve from the shop's root —
  Shopify strips the header that would allow it. The install sheet explains
  the menu route instead of waiting for a banner that will not come.

  Status bar style is "black", not "black-translucent": translucent runs the
  page under the clock and needs safe-area padding on every fixed element,
  for a status bar that would be near-black either way.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="manifest" href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=crk-manifest">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#0B0A0E">
<meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="{{ settings.crk_app_short_name | default: shop.name | escape }}">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ 'crooks-apple-touch-icon.png' | asset_url }}">
